1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,880
Thirty silver coins hit the temple floor.

2
00:00:02,601 --> 00:00:04,461
Each one lands on a mark written five hundred

3
00:00:04,501 --> 00:00:05,061
years early.

4
00:00:05,241 --> 00:00:07,922
Five centuries before, Zechariah asked Israel

5
00:00:07,982 --> 00:00:09,102
for his shepherd's wages.

6
00:00:09,603 --> 00:00:11,963
So they weighed for my price thirty pieces

7
00:00:12,023 --> 00:00:12,503
of silver.

8
00:00:12,543 --> 00:00:13,243
Thirty shekels.

9
00:00:13,804 --> 00:00:15,244
The law's price for a slave.

10
00:00:16,244 --> 00:00:17,745
The LORD took it personally.

11
00:00:18,345 --> 00:00:20,765
A goodly price that I was prised at of them.

12
00:00:20,906 --> 00:00:23,106
And Zechariah threw them where the LORD said.

13
00:00:23,626 --> 00:00:25,887
And I took the thirty pieces of silver, and

14
00:00:25,927 --> 00:00:27,887
cast them to the potter in the house of the

15
00:00:27,927 --> 00:00:28,227
LORD.

16
00:00:28,387 --> 00:00:30,528
Then Judas sold Jesus for the same sum.

17
00:00:31,068 --> 00:00:32,929
And he cast down the pieces of silver in the

18
00:00:32,989 --> 00:00:34,269
temple, and departed.

19
00:00:34,389 --> 00:00:34,949
Cast down.

20
00:00:35,749 --> 00:00:36,310
In the temple.

21
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:38,030
The priests took it.

22
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:39,310
Blood money.

23
00:00:40,271 --> 00:00:41,391
It bought the potter's field.

24
00:00:41,611 --> 00:00:43,331
Nobody was trying to fulfil prophecy.

25
00:00:44,092 --> 00:00:45,532
Every coin found its mark.

26
00:00:45,672 --> 00:00:46,952
The cross was no accident.

27
00:00:47,813 --> 00:00:49,893
Jesus let himself be weighed like a slave.

28
00:00:50,353 --> 00:00:51,934
The silver bought a field for the dead.

29
00:00:52,834 --> 00:00:53,994
His blood bought you back.

30
00:00:54,754 --> 00:00:56,075
Stop weighing out your own price.

31
00:00:56,795 --> 00:00:58,956
Receive his price, and go free.
